0.13735421001911163, "top": [["-linux", -0.13735421001911163], ["`)", -2.6168463230133057]]}, {"t": "-gnu", "lp": -0.0013743542367592454, "top": [["-gnu", -0.0013743542367592454], ["-gun", -6.767155647277832]]}, {"t": "`)", "lp": -0.031035972759127617, "top": [["`)", -0.031035972759127617], ["`", -4.172633647918701]]}, {"t": "\n\n", "lp": -0.0018385254079475999, "top": [["\n\n", -0.0018385254079475999], [" \u2014", -6.524788856506348]]}, {"t": "```", "lp": -0.06251020729541779, "top": [["```", -0.06251020729541779], ["##", -3.1248385906219482]]}, {"t": "bash", "lp": -0.0011240001767873764, "top": [["bash", -0.0011240001767873764], ["\n", -7.308473587036133]]}, {"t": "\n", "lp": -0.0013017778983339667, "top": [["\n", -0.0013017778983339667], [" -", -8.826922416687012]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set up even if it appears already configured. This is essential because we're using Intel's `icx`/`icpx` compilers, which aren't on the default PATH.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nThis makes the script exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero (error) status. A safety net so a failed command doesn't cascade into broken output.\n\n## The CMake Configuration\n\nNow the main `cmake` command. Let me flag by flag:\n\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja\n```\n- `-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"` \u2014 **source directory** (where the CMakeLists.txt lives)\n- `-B \"${srcdir}/build\"` \u2014 **build directory** (where all compiled artifacts go)\n- `-G Ninja` \u2014 use the **Ninja** build generator (fast, minimal output) instead of the default Makefiles\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\n```\nOptimize for performance (`-O3`, strip debug symbols). This is the production build type.\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib\n```\n- Install binaries to `/usr`\n- Install libraries to `/usr/lib` (rather than the default `/usr/lib64` or `/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu`)\n\n```bash\n"}